  "question": {
    "text": "Let $A B C D$ be a trapezium whose vertices lie on the parabola $y^2=4 x$. Let the sides $A D$ and $B C$ of the trapezium be parallel to y -axis. If the diagonal AC is of length $\\frac{25}{4}$ and it passes through the point $(1,0)$, then the area of $A B C D$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "w2hnd",
      "text": "$\\frac{75}{4}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "aHu2q",
      "text": "$\\frac{25}{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JUNyO",
      "text": "$\\frac{125}{8}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "7ylmn",
      "text": "$\\frac{75}{8}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/RtE3cdTR4nN8ytMvAsisJbjNTGJ45PcE9G1pIcAKLmc.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\n\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{A}\\left(\\mathrm{at}_1^2, 2 \\mathrm{at}\\right) \\& \\mathrm{C}\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{a}}{\\mathrm{t}_1^2},-\\frac{2 \\mathrm{a}}{\\mathrm{t}_1}\\right) \\\\\n& \\text { Length } \\mathrm{AC}=\\mathrm{a}\\left(\\mathrm{t}_1+\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{t}_1}\\right)^2=\\frac{25}{4}, \\mathrm{t}_1+\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{t}_1}= \\pm \\frac{5}{2} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{t}_1=2 \\text { or } \\frac{1}{2}, \\mathrm{~A}\\left(\\frac{1}{2}, 1\\right), \\mathrm{D}\\left(\\frac{1}{4},-1\\right), \\mathrm{B}(4,4), \\mathrm{C}(4,-4)\n\\end{aligned}$\n\nSo, area of trapezium $=\\frac{1}{2}(8+2)\\left(4-\\frac{1}{4}\\right)=\\frac{75}{4}$",
    "image": null
  },
